# Sensitive paths for shipping-work's doc-check.sh (Step 1.5).
#
# Files whose existence, names, or structure is mirrored in AGENTS.md / README.md
# / docs/. When one changes, the matching doc section probably needs updating too.
#
# Grammar: one path per line; blank lines and #-comments ignored. Entries match
# whole path SEGMENTS at any depth, not a root-anchored prefix — `core/` matches
# `src/address_validator/core/`. This file REPLACES the skill's built-in
# defaults rather than extending them (gregoryfoster/skills#252, GH #208).
#
# Why tailored: the defaults describe a `src/api|models|core/` service. This repo
# is a flat `src/address_validator/` package, so 6 of the 12 default entries
# (schema.sql, deploy/, src/api/, src/models/, src/core/, .env.example) matched
# nothing and Step 1.5 passed without being able to fail.
#
# Every entry below must match at least one tracked file. That is enforced, not
# asserted — re-verify after any layout change with:
#   uv run pytest tests/unit/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py
#
# Do NOT re-verify with `doc-check.sh --base HEAD`. An empty diff returns at
# "No changes vs ..." before the dead-entry census runs, so it reports a green
# without inspecting a single entry. The census is on the no-hit path only: to
# see it by hand, pass a --base whose diff touches nothing in this list.

# Deliberately absent: docs/. docs/plans/ and docs/research/ are dated snapshots
# that churn on every design cycle, and a segment-matching list has no way to
# exclude them — an entry for docs/ would hit on nearly every branch and train
# the reader to ignore Step 1.5.
#
# Also absent: templates/ and static/. docs/STYLE.md is a rulebook (brand, dark
# mode, WCAG 2.1 AA), not an inventory of them — the coupling is too weak to
# earn a hit on every admin-dashboard tweak.

# --- Doc surface itself, including the entrypoint that loads it ---
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md
CHANGELOG.md

